      "summary": "The CMap and repeated-stream checks address the prior findings, but page-letter materialization still precedes the text guard and can create substantial allocations from a bounded text stream.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Evidence/IsolatedPdfParser.cs",
          "line": 138,
          "message": "The page-text guard still runs after PdfPig materializes page letters. The new stream byte cap does not bound the memory used by a large letter collection, leaving the previously reported extraction resource risk reachable.",
          "confidence": 0.84,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "ParseCore enumerates getTextParts(page), which accesses page.Letters, before CanMaterializePageText checks the accumulated text. The preflight caps text stream bytes, but does not cap the number of PdfPig letter objects created from those bytes.",
            "failureScenario": "A PDF with a text stream near the 512 KiB limit containing many glyphs passes preflight. PdfPig materializes a large page.Letters collection while getTextParts is enumerated, before the text guard can reject it; concurrent submissions can put excessive memory pressure on the API process (OWASP A06:2025)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
